WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:03.330
Stella!

3
00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:05.200
Are you there?

4
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.250
Ohh... goodness gracious.

5
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.070
Those darn seraphim
trashed this place!

6
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.100
You'd think they'd show some
respect for the lab they were born in.

7
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.650
I'll have to give them
a stern talking to.

8
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:19.200
Huh?

9
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:19.920
Hm?

10
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:26.530
An explosion?

11
00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.270
Pythagoras! What happened?

12
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:30.530
What was that noise?

13
00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.710
Pythagoras! Do you copy?

14
00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.220
Come in, Pythagoras!

15
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.730
Where are you?

16
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:36.970
Answer me, please!

17
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.430
What is happening?

18
00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:16.030
<b>LABOPHASE DEATH GAME</b>

19
00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.160
Building C.

20
00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.150
Camsnail 12.

21
00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.180
Scan the area for signs of life.

22
00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.440
Your mission is
to locate Pythagoras.

23
00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.290
Was there an accident?

24
00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:26.790
Please, let him be safe.

25
00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:31.580
Huh?

26
00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.070
There's something there!

27
00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:35.380
A shadow!

28
00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:41.660
Answer me!

29
00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.220
They destroyed
the Camps now.

30
00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.580
Everything all right?

31
00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.730
This stupid ear thing's broken.

32
00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.040
Where are you going?

33
00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.770
I'm gonna go talk
to Helmet Guy for a minute.

34
00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.070
<b>Building A</b>

35
00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.320
<b>Building C Building B</b>

36
00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:03.080
<b>Third Floor
Building A</b>

37
00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.480
Come on, we have to go!

38
00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.050
Vegapunk!

39
00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:06.160
Jeez, can we catch
a break for once?

40
00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:08.440
I don't even know
where to start.

41
00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.940
This place is enormous!

42
00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.480
Yeah, tell me about it.

43
00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.440
You wouldn't believe how long it takes
us to play hide and seek in here.

44
00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:15.160
Vegapunk!

45
00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:17.710
Wha...?

46
00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:21.670
Vegapunk!

47
00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:22.910
What's that face?

48
00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:23.980
Did you find something?

49
00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.760
I sure did!

50
00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.920
Uh! What?

51
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:26.860
What is it?

52
00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:31.740
So shiny!

53
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:33.240
Diamonds?

54
00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.120
That's what you're
focused on?

55
00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.280
They're all mine!

56
00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:38.620
Are you kidding me?

57
00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.610
At least say They're so pretty!
Or something normal!

58
00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:42.710
Yo!

59
00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.320
Come on, let her have this.

60
00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.750
What does it matter?

61
00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.820
You're leaving the island
anyway, aren't you?

62
00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.500
Shouldn't let 'em go to waste!

63
00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.410
That is not the issue here!

64
00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.020
There's something wrong
with her priorities!

65
00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.360
We have to debug her!

66
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:55.240
Oh, boy.

67
00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.120
Heavy.

68
00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.000
Maybe we should head
back now.

69
00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:01.270
We're supposed to be
looking for Stella!

70
00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:06.030
Okay, okay, fine.

71
00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.480
I'll set it down for now,

72
00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.780
but you'd better lead us
through here on our way back!

73
00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.800
You behave while
mommy's gone!

74
00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:14.530
I'll come back for you soon!

75
00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:17.980
Just so you know, those
are man-made diamonds.

76
00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.640
They're for industrial use.

77
00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:20.640
What?

78
00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.640
Can you make diamonds?

79
00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:24.730
This place is paradise!

80
00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:27.480
What's wrong with your eyes?

81
00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.030
The future is full of dreams!

82
00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:32.170
These people are maniacs!

83
00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.780
Stella, please,
come out already!

84
00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:42.110
I just wish our tour was under
less stressful circumstances.

85
00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.370
Atlas? Quick question.

86
00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:48.850
Lucci really smashed up your face,
but now it looks great!

87
00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:55.070
<b>Second Floor
Building A</b>

88
00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.710
Does it work like a mask?

89
00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.430
In the future, you can make
your body how you want!

90
00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:55.500
Replacing some parts is easy!

91
00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:56.430
What's this?

92
00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:57.310
A creature?

93
00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.100
Or Vegapunk, perhaps?

94
00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:00.270
Vegapunk?

95
00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.190
Where?

96
00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:01.770
What?

97
00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:02.700
No!

98
00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.670
That's what we
call an organoid.

99
00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.480
It's an artificial organ!

100
00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:08.880
Fascinating.

101
00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.030
This technology is vital
to the future of medicine!

102
00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:12.910
Really?

103
00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.590
You can make organs
all on your own?

104
00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:16.480
Amazing!

105
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.100
How wonderful.

106
00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.170
This will certainly save lives.

107
00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.700
And what a relief, too!

108
00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:24.300
I thought it was
something else.

109
00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.380
Huh?

110
00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:28.290
A dismembered piece of Vegapunk
put on gruesome display.

111
00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:30.180
Why would you
even think that?!

112
00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.500
Hey! Helmet Guy!

113
00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.350
This is completely absurd.

114
00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.610
Edison! This is Shaka!

115
00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:38.740
Please respond!

116
00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.360
Did something bad happen?

117
00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:43.410
<b>Control Room
Fourth Floor
Building A</b>

118
00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.880
I've lost contact
with the other Satellites.

119
00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.530
Oh, your thing break, too?

120
00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:48.530
I was talkin' to everybody fine a second
ago, but then it got all messed up.

121
00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.490
Now I'm not gettin'
anything at all.

122
00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:54.210
But, uh... I didn't break it,
honestly, I swear!

123
00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:55.990
That's not what I...

124
00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:56.820
No, seriously!

125
00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:57.920
It stayed here!

126
00:05:58.390 --> 00:05:59.420
On my head!

127
00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:01.020
You misunderstand.

128
00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:02.610
Observe.

129
00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.170
The video feeds
are shutting off,

130
00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.900
One after another,
after another.

131
00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:16.430
Fuck!

132
00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:17.400
But why?

133
00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.650
Someone is
interfering with them.

134
00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:21.940
We have an intruder.

135
00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.730
Dr. Vegapunk!

136
00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.430
Where are you?

137
00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:29.980
I still can't believe you and I
get to go on a voyage together!

138
00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:30.800
Wow!

139
00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.290
You were at Big Mom's
party, weren't you?

140
00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:36.830
I'll do anything!

141
00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.790
Please tell me I'm a good boy!

142
00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:42.520
Let's get serious
and look for Stella.

143
00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:43.910
Silly puppy.

144
00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:46.400
We can't search every
nook and cranny.

145
00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:48.390
The lab is entirely too big.

146
00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:49.710
This'll take all day.

147
00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:54.100
<b>Second Floor
Building B (Right)</b>

148
00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:54.350
We're on a weapons development floor,
so don't set off any shock waves.

149
00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:00.010
Hello?!

150
00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:01.010
Vegapunk!

151
00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.110
Come on, Vegapunk!

152
00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:04.090
It's time to go!

153
00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.280
<b>Third Floor
Building C (Left)</b>

154
00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.080
Uh-uh. Keep those eyes open, York!

155
00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:12.680
Wake up!

156
00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:13.400
Fine.

157
00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:17.670
Where could he have
wandered off to?

158
00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.490
And why did he have
to disappear now?

159
00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:21.670
The Government will
be after us any second!

160
00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.120
Then let's use this!

161
00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:25.680
Ah! I got a wife and kids!

162
00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:27.350
Chill, it's a Bubble Gun.

163
00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:29.910
Hm? What's a Bubble Gun?

164
00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:31.120
It sounds cool!

165
00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.240
You bet it is!

166
00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.260
Wait till you see it pop off!

167
00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:37.320
Its attack
can deflect anything!

168
00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:45.990
You said attack, but it
sounds more like a shield.

169
00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.370
You'd understand if
you saw it in action.

170
00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:50.430
Would you like
a demonstration?

171
00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:51.650
Oh, for real?

172
00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:54.320
If it's made by Vegapunk,
I bet it's super sweet.

173
00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.350
Show me what
this baby can do!

174
00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:58.900
Wow, you're really
into this, huh?

175
00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.270
Huh?

176
00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:04.620
Hey, guys?

177
00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:05.530
What's that?

178
00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:09.820
You see something?

179
00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.250
Do you have eyes on Stella?

180
00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:12.890
No, it's smoke.

181
00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.280
Something blew up.

182
00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:15.470
Whoa!

183
00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:17.000
The whole bridge is out!

184
00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.210
What happened?

185
00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:19.500
Is it the baddies?

186
00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:21.270
This just keeps getting worse!

187
00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.830
What's going on here?

188
00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:29.320
There's someone on the floor!

189
00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.040
What?

190
00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.190
It can't be!

191
00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:36.830
Pythagoras!

192
00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:39.320
Hey, stay with me, buddy!

193
00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:40.650
Are you okay?

194
00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:44.900
Gah! He's been decapitated!

195
00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:46.090
This is sick.

196
00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:48.440
His whole head musta
been blown clean off!

197
00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:51.620
Oh, man, this must have been
the explosion that we heard earlier!

198
00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:54.650
Pythagoras? Wiggle your fingers
if you can hear me!

199
00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:57.390
Who's there?

200
00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:58.860
Don't shoot!

201
00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.230
I come in peace!

202
00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:02.940
Yellow, everybody!

203
00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.340
Wait a sec, is that...?

204
00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:05.810
Pythagoras!

205
00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.360
You're alive!

206
00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.900
And you're a football!

207
00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.990
Who did this to you?

208
00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.850
It couldn't have been
an accident, right?

209
00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:16.640
'Cause you look like you've
been stripped for parts!

210
00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:17.550
Huh?

211
00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:19.180
I don't know!

212
00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.580
It's very confusing!

213
00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.750
That is to say,
I saw the culprit,

214
00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.050
but, well, I-it was, uh...

215
00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:26.860
Come on, man.
Just spit it out!

216
00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.440
Yeah, maybe I made
a design error.

217
00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.400
No, I promised myself I'd
work on my confidence.

218
00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:32.980
Hey!

219
00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:33.860
Focus!

220
00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:37.340
Where's York?

221
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:38.810
Hi, baby!

222
00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.830
What are you doing here?

223
00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.560
I thought Edison
told you to stay put!

224
00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.860
You're supposed to be
waiting for us outside, goofy.

225
00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:48.020
Oh, but you're...

226
00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.430
You're so cute!

227
00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:52.740
Uh.

228
00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:53.550
Hey, York!

229
00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:54.880
What are you doing?

230
00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:59.340
You guys, look!

231
00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:01.450
I found a little cutie over here!

232
00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:08.210
Love-Love...

233
00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:11.400
Love-Love...

234
00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.130
It can't be!

235
00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.270
Why? We gave you a new command!

236
00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:37.010
Try again!

237
00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:38.610
She's getting closer!

238
00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:41.150
Seraphim. Stay right there!

239
00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:46.370
Why aren't you
listening to me?

240
00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:51.770
Do you...

241
00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:23.570
Luffy, quick!

242
00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:24.310
I need help!

243
00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:26.670
I gotcha!

244
00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:27.860
What's up?

245
00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:35.560
Aren't those guys supposed
to be on our side?

246
00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:37.370
Seraphim!

247
00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:38.610
S-Hawk.

248
00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:39.760
S-Bear.

249
00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:40.330
Bear!

250
00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:43.960
Abort all assault operations!

251
00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:45.980
Who gave you
the command to attack?

252
00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:48.650
Is that really all it
takes to stop them?

253
00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.730
Don't know why, but they
were coming after CP0.

254
00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:55.190
I didn't wanna let them
die handcuffed like that.

255
00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:57.800
It woulda left a bad
taste in my mouth.

256
00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:13.650
No, wait!

257
00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:15.010
They're not listening to me!

258
00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:15.920
No!

259
00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:22.870
I told you!

260
00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:26.650
I regret everything!

261
00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:28.500
She hears us,
but she doesn't obey!

262
00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.010
Hover! Quick!

263
00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:32.490
Turn on your Dom Shoes!

264
00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:33.370
Roger!

265
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.180
I got it!

266
00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:42.690
Uh-oh!

267
00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:43.240
No I don't!

268
00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.350
Somebody help!

269
00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:45.000
Oh, no!

270
00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.660
Catch me!

271
00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:54.890
Aaaaah!

272
00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:57.420
Is this heaven?

273
00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.180
Take me home, sweet angels.

274
00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:00.060
Shaka?

275
00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:01.470
Hey!

276
00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.400
Answer me!

277
00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:04.720
It's no use!

278
00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:07.180
Communications are
out all over the lab!

279
00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:08.060
What?

280
00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:13.740
Well damn!

281
00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:16.670
I was really hopin'
that would work!

282
00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.600
Is it cool to fight back?

283
00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:22.530
'Cause if so, I'mma
give her a wallop!

284
00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:22.750
Whoa!

285
00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:23.830
Are you kidding me?

286
00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:24.440
No!

287
00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.810
You need to stay away,
for your own good!

288
00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:27.870
She'll kill you!

289
00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:29.570
She's our masterpiece.

290
00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.730
The strongest
form of humanity!

291
00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:53.010
Oh, whoa!

292
00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:55.180
That was too close!

293
00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:55.900
Indeed.

294
00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.930
There is something
terribly wrong here.

295
00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:01.480
Despite
my authority level,

296
00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:04.190
the seraphim won't
respond to my commands.

297
00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:07.110
Which leaves only one
possible explanation.

298
00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:10.610
They're receiving orders...
from another Vegapunk.

299
00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:16.450
Huh?

300
00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:19.140
It's all beginning
to make sense.

301
00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:20.720
Our comms failed us.

302
00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:24.230
And we were caged by
our own security system.

303
00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.370
It was all by design.

304
00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:29.600
We have a traitor
in our midst,

305
00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:32.770
and they want every
one of us dead.

306
00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:33.020
What?!

307
00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.820
That includes us
it would seem.

308
00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:40.920
I would tear those
things apart if I could.

309
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.150
But it's no use.

310
00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:43.050
We're trapped.

311
00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:47.660
Alright. Hey,
Straw Hat, Roronoa.

312
00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:49.530
What do you say
the four of us call a truce

313
00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:51.500
and try to work together?

314
00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.320
We'll establish
a temporary alliance.

315
00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.060
All you have to do
is uncuff us.

316
00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:01.020
And let us do
what we do best.

317
00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:08.800
They're disgusted.

318
00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:16.770
Let's say we do uncuff you guys,
and you help us win this fight...

319
00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:21.760
You expect us to believe you're just gonna
let us cuff you again when it's over?

320
00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:23.770
We have no reason
to lie to you.

321
00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:27.510
Our only objective now is
getting out of this alive.

322
00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:31.680
Let us help, and we'll let you cuff
us again when we're through.

323
00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:33.040
Okay, cool.

324
00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:34.890
We'll take the cuffs off, then!

325
00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:35.840
What?!

326
00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:39.830
That was clearly
just bullshit, Luffy!

327
00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:56.180
Wait a sec.

328
00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:58.910
That's the bald guy's move!

329
00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:03.280
He has the power
of the Dice-Dice Fruit.

330
00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:13.700
<b>Inside the Laboratory</b>

331
00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:16.740
We need food.

332
00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.510
It's been two months.

333
00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.040
Two months without
a proper meal.

334
00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:32.980
We're done for.

335
00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.470
We're going to die in here.

336
00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:38.310
<b>CP5, CP7, and CP8
World Government
Intelligence Agents</b>

337
00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:39.800
Two months ago...

338
00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:42.650
We completed
our investigation here.

339
00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:45.830
We left the island like normal,

340
00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:49.060
But we were attacked by
the Sea Beast Weapons.

341
00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:52.800
So we headed
back to the island.

342
00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:56.280
Cipher Pol sent backup
when we didn't return,

343
00:16:56.360 --> 00:17:00.630
but as you can see, they got
stuffed in this room, same as us.

344
00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:05.530
This whole time we all assumed
you were the mastermind.

345
00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:08.570
I'm sorry, Dr. Vegapunk.

346
00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:14.720
No. I'm sorry.

347
00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:17.980
I was completely
blind to the truth.

348
00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:20.580
Egghead is my lab.

349
00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:25.520
I allowed this to happen
under my own roof.

350
00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:28.110
What a fool I was.

351
00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.540
Why didn't I see the signs?

352
00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:33.710
It should have
been impossible.

353
00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:39.040
For the Government to find
out about my research.

354
00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.420
Naval Branch G9!

355
00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.330
All ships have been deployed!

356
00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.710
Counting all sizes,

357
00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.800
The total number of vessels
currently en route to Egghead...

358
00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.680
Now exceeds 100!

359
00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:52.510
Understood.

360
00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:06.470
Zoro. Do you recognize
that devil fruit power?

361
00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:07.100
Uh-huh.

362
00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:09.530
Back when we fought
Baroque Works.

363
00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:18.540
It's a full-body blade power.

364
00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:05.070
What did
you do with Lucci?

365
00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:06.180
I dropped him over there.

366
00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:07.130
You what?!

367
00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:31.970
Okay, that's it!

368
00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:40.030
There, see? We told you!

369
00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:46.180
You can't protect us and win
against those things!

370
00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:49.140
You have to let us help
you before it's too late!

371
00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:51.600
Cp zero.

372
00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.100
Tell me the truth.

373
00:19:56.140 --> 00:19:57.380
What is your mission?

374
00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:02.040
The elimination
of Doctor Vegapunk.

375
00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:04.290
All seven of you.

376
00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:05.610
What is wrong with you?!

377
00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:07.650
How could you say
that to his face?

378
00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:10.040
Hmm.
And what about Stussy,

379
00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:11.940
who betrayed you to help us?

380
00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:14.560
I don't suppose you'll
let her off easily.

381
00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:18.220
That's right. She'll get
what's coming to her.

382
00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:21.490
Just digging our graves deeper
and deeper, aren't you?

383
00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:22.970
Nami!

384
00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:27.040
<b>Third Floor, Building A</b>

385
00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:28.740
Huh?

386
00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:30.480
Huh?!

387
00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:36.780
Run for your lives!

388
00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.010
That was
Nami's scream.

389
00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.290
There must be more
seraphim here.

390
00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:53.820
<b>Third Floor, Building C</b>

391
00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:11.650
It's probably all four
of 'em. No one is safe.

392
00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:20.400
There's seven Vegapunks
we gotta look out for.

393
00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:24.230
Plus, uh... how many more?

394
00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:36.200
That power.

395
00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:39.060
Helmet Guy.

396
00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:43.440
I need the keys.

397
00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:45.210
Huh?

398
00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:49.760
Very well.
I trust your judgment.

399
00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:56.290
Straw Hat Luffy.

400
00:21:58.050 --> 00:22:02.040
Promise me that you
will protect Stella at any cost.

401
00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:04.970
No prob! You got it!

402
00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:11.820
Hey! We're gonna
stop all four seraphim.

403
00:22:11.860 --> 00:22:13.590
You gonna be a jerk
when we're done?

404
00:22:13.620 --> 00:22:15.090
You're not gonna try
to hurt my friends

405
00:22:15.090 --> 00:22:17.160
just 'cause you can't
beat me, right?

406
00:22:17.210 --> 00:22:18.400
Oh, come on!

407
00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:21.790
You really think provoking
him like that's gonna work?

408
00:22:21.820 --> 00:22:23.640
I don't care about them!

409
00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:26.630
The only thing that matters
to me right now is killing you.

410
00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:28.060
Straw Hat!

411
00:22:28.090 --> 00:22:30.030
So, no, I won't
kill your friends.

412
00:22:30.110 --> 00:22:32.780
Not until after I've buried
you once and for all!

413
00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:35.090
Huh. It did work!

414
00:22:35.090 --> 00:22:36.120
Okay!

415
00:22:37.090 --> 00:22:40.670
Hey, hey, hey, hey!
We've got an emergency here!

416
00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:41.900
Ursus...

417
00:22:43.930 --> 00:22:44.810
Shock.

418
00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:02.610
Fourth Gear!
Bounce Man!

419
00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:05.140
Time to finish this!

420
00:23:08.310 --> 00:23:09.910
I'm sorry, Bonney.

421
00:23:11.300 --> 00:23:12.390
Here we go!

422
00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:28.950
Don't get in my way.

423
00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:31.090
Who do you
think you're talking to?

424
00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:35.860
Purgatory... Oni Giri!

425
00:23:35.860 --> 00:23:39.020
Tempest Kick! White Thunder!

426
00:23:54.840 --> 00:23:55.960
Gum-Gum...

427
00:23:56.860 --> 00:23:57.840
Six King...

428
00:23:58.110 --> 00:24:01.070
...Kong...

429
00:24:01.360 --> 00:24:02.190
– ...Gun!
– ...Pistol!

430
00:24:36.070 --> 00:24:38.970
On an island
somewhere in the New World...

431
00:24:43.770 --> 00:24:46.310
...a familiar
scene plays out in a bar.

432
00:24:46.530 --> 00:24:48.870
Come on,
don't be so stingy!

433
00:24:48.870 --> 00:24:51.310
I'm not kiddin'
around here, okay?

434
00:24:51.610 --> 00:24:53.470
I told you, I wanna go.

435
00:24:53.580 --> 00:24:55.750
So why won't you
take me with you?

436
00:24:55.830 --> 00:24:57.330
Let me on your ship!

437
00:24:57.410 --> 00:24:58.970
Not a chance.

438
00:24:58.970 --> 00:25:01.370
But we have a strict "no
hotheaded brats" rule.

439
00:25:01.810 --> 00:25:03.590
Sorry, it's just policy.

440
00:25:07.090 --> 00:25:08.660
Better stop while
you're ahead.

441
00:25:08.730 --> 00:25:10.030
Keep this up and our captains

442
00:25:10.170 --> 00:25:11.710
are going to get
their feelings hurt!

443
00:25:11.810 --> 00:25:12.650
I don't care!

444
00:25:12.750 --> 00:25:15.340
Shanks is the only
one I wanna sail with!

445
00:25:15.470 --> 00:25:17.370
I've been getting
stronger, by the way!

446
00:25:17.370 --> 00:25:19.530
I'll be your best
crew member in no time!

447
00:25:19.780 --> 00:25:21.510
You gotta take me, please!

448
00:25:21.340 --> 00:25:24.640
Say something already!
You're pissing me off!

449
00:25:24.870 --> 00:25:26.840
All this yelling just
proves me right.

450
00:25:26.850 --> 00:25:31.270
Oh,
come on! This sucks!

451
00:25:35.310 --> 00:25:37.710
I'm real sorry
to interrupt you, Chief!

452
00:25:37.790 --> 00:25:38.990
We need help!

453
00:25:40.110 --> 00:25:41.410
But we got hit!

454
00:25:41.490 --> 00:25:43.420
That bastard wants
another fight!

455
00:25:43.420 --> 00:25:44.710
A bunch of the younger
guys are angry

456
00:25:44.710 --> 00:25:46.630
they got blindsided like that.

457
00:25:47.030 --> 00:25:48.940
And now they're
looking for blood!

458
00:25:49.020 --> 00:25:50.420
What do we do?

459
00:25:50.500 --> 00:25:53.270
I'm thinking this might
turn into a big battle!

460
00:25:57.350 --> 00:25:58.520
Well, damn.

461
00:25:59.290 --> 00:26:01.810
I'm not sure if
their timing's good or bad.

462
00:26:01.810 --> 00:26:06.750
We were just about to sail
our way outta here.

463
00:26:06.940 --> 00:26:09.880
Seems I got carried away
and chatted for too long.

464
00:26:10.730 --> 00:26:11.810
But it's not every day

465
00:26:11.810 --> 00:26:15.190
you get to see an old friend
you thought was dead.

466
00:26:15.750 --> 00:26:17.550
What choice did I have?

467
00:26:18.610 --> 00:26:20.790
Our enemy does have
quite the temper.

468
00:26:20.860 --> 00:26:23.750
That's rich,
comin' from you!

469
00:26:23.750 --> 00:26:26.690
Who'd you think pissed
him off in the first place?

470
00:26:27.440 --> 00:26:28.810
Time to set sail.

471
00:26:28.890 --> 00:26:30.710
Now that's what I like to hear!

472
00:26:30.750 --> 00:26:33.230
Yeah!

473
00:26:33.230 --> 00:26:35.510
You're going to war?
Oh, wow!

474
00:26:35.510 --> 00:26:38.570
I won't let Elbaph
become a battlefield.

475
00:26:38.720 --> 00:26:40.460
Oh! What a man!

476
00:26:41.420 --> 00:26:44.740
Our duty is to keep
this island safe from harm.

477
00:26:46.730 --> 00:26:53.150
This is a proud
country of warriors: Elbaph.

478
00:27:01.070 --> 00:27:03.100
You'll help
us protect the place,

479
00:27:03.190 --> 00:27:05.230
right, Dorry, Brogy?

480
00:27:05.230 --> 00:27:09.110
It would be
my pleasure, brother.

481
00:27:09.240 --> 00:27:12.150
It looks
like you're fired up!

482
00:27:18.910 --> 00:27:22.810
Hey, before we get into this,
go ask him a question.

483
00:27:22.810 --> 00:27:25.290
Captain
Kid, you mean? What is it?

484
00:27:25.780 --> 00:27:28.420
This is about
to be a turning point for him.

485
00:27:31.550 --> 00:27:34.440
Ask if he
really wants to fight me.

486
00:27:34.520 --> 00:27:36.320
Because there is another way.

487
00:27:36.320 --> 00:27:37.530
If he leaves
his Road Poneglyphs behind,

488
00:27:37.530 --> 00:27:39.360
I'll let him go.

489
00:27:39.820 --> 00:27:41.120
It's his choice.

490
00:27:47.480 --> 00:27:50.400
<b>Elbaph, the Land of War
New World</b>

491
00:27:58.490 --> 00:28:00.650
Looks like those
ships lined up on the shore

492
00:28:00.650 --> 00:28:02.160
are our enemies,

493
00:28:02.700 --> 00:28:05.490
along with these
jackasses shooting at us.

494
00:28:06.490 --> 00:28:08.040
But why, you ask?

495
00:28:08.080 --> 00:28:09.960
Because they're all
from pirate crews

496
00:28:09.960 --> 00:28:13.750
that serve under the wing
of Red-Haired Shanks.

497
00:28:13.820 --> 00:28:16.300
Each one of them is
known and feared.

498
00:28:18.880 --> 00:28:20.390
Glad you could make it, Chief!

499
00:28:20.860 --> 00:28:23.630
We're so happy to see
your handsome face again!

500
00:28:24.300 --> 00:28:25.520
And Beckman, too!

501
00:28:27.940 --> 00:28:29.950
Hey,
don't get too close to the boss!

502
00:28:30.030 --> 00:28:32.140
Let us pay you a tribute
while you're here!

503
00:28:32.300 --> 00:28:35.550
Aw, thanks, but we don't
work like that, old pal!

504
00:28:44.390 --> 00:28:47.110
Last time, we never
got our shot at Shanks.

505
00:28:47.110 --> 00:28:50.680
His crew sent us packing before
we even caught a glimpse of him.

506
00:28:50.680 --> 00:28:53.900
Well, after teaching
us a lesson, that is.

507
00:28:59.800 --> 00:29:02.210
Guess I don't need
to remind you, though.

508
00:29:14.400 --> 00:29:16.690
But taking
your arm was just a warning.

509
00:29:26.970 --> 00:29:29.920
Now, they'll
be coming for your life.

510
00:29:47.540 --> 00:29:49.290
They'll try, I'm sure.

511
00:29:52.640 --> 00:29:53.690
But this time,

512
00:29:53.690 --> 00:29:58.030
they're going to be the ones
leaving empty-handed!
